{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes","id":1010906,"title":"Aimed spells and successes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-01T19:33:10-08:00","id":1010906,"title":"Aimed spells and successes","content":"My search-fu is weak, I tried but could not find an answer so I come to you.<br /> <br /> If I am attacking someone with a Fireball spell that does 3 bashing damage. I roll Dex + Athletics/Firearms - Defense to hit.... If I get two successes am I doing 5 or 3 damage?<br /> <br /> Thanks for any help : )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T19:42:31-08:00","id":1010907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes#post1010906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My search-fu is weak, I tried but could not find an answer so I come to you.<br /> <br /> If I am attacking someone with a Fireball spell that does 3 bashing damage. I roll Dex + Athletics/Firearms - Defense to hit.... If I get two successes am I doing 5 or 3 damage?<br /> <br /> Thanks for any help : )</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a fireball spell would deal damage according to the fire rules. But assuming some other direct damage spell, let's say Rotting Flesh or something, it would do 3 damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T19:47:28-08:00","id":1010910,"title":"","content":"What Charlaquin said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T21:13:21-08:00","id":1010925,"title":"","content":"How accurate your spell slinging is has nothing to do with how much damage it does if you hit your target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T21:48:39-08:00","id":1010929,"title":"","content":"Personally I rather like the idea that it does, it would encourage Mages to fling their attack spells at each other and the image of fireballs flying at dodging opponents is far more exciting than frequent belching from unseen heartburn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T22:06:11-08:00","id":1010935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1010929#post1010929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I rather like the idea that it does, it would encourage Mages to fling their attack spells at each other</div> </div> </div> </div>They're already encouraged to do that \u2014 sensory range costs a Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T22:14:25-08:00","id":1010938,"title":"","content":"Yea, but it would encourage them more.<br /> \u200bBesides with the way potency currently works if you're like me and need to roll at least twelve dice to count on getting one success, anything that helps is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T23:39:37-08:00","id":1010957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1010938#post1010938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBesides with the way potency currently works</div> </div> </div> </div>The way Potency currently works for &quot;attack spells&quot; is that casting it at the default range gives you a hefty rock to throw that deals splash damage if you bother with Scale factors.<br /> <br /> Having enough dots in an Arcanum to cast a standard-issue Unraveling spell means a basic instant-casting gives you a +4L thrown weapon, and pumping more damage into that projectile has zero impact on your ability to hit a given target because the aiming roll is separate from the casting roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T00:51:11-08:00","id":1010968,"title":"","content":"In order to do what you want, you need a spell that creates a Weapon Equivalent with Damage Rating equal to Potency (probably for X uses). This shouldn't be too hard to Creative Thaumaturgy-ize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T01:45:54-08:00","id":1010979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1010968#post1010968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order to do what you want, you need a spell that creates a Weapon Equivalent with Damage Rating equal to Potency (probably for X uses). This shouldn't be too hard to Creative Thaumaturgy-ize.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1 Reach: Create a 'physical' manifestation of the spell that attacks using Desterity+Weaponry/Brawl-Defense, extra successes does not add to the damage dealt. Split Potency between damage and uses, running out of uses ends the spell. Using it in sensory range allows you to attack from range but still requires an attack roll but do not apply penalties to it from the Arm Wrack tilt and can still attack while Immobilized<br /> <br /> Apply it to the direct damage spells, boom! done.<br /> (Note, first Creative Thaumaturgying)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T02:10:55-08:00","id":1010983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>backtoback</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1010979#post1010979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+1 Reach: Create a 'physical' manifestation of the spell that attacks using Desterity+Weaponry/Brawl-Defense, extra successes does not add to the damage dealt. Split Potency between damage and uses, running out of uses ends the spell. Using it in sensory range allows you to attack from range but still requires an attack roll but do not apply penalties to it from the Arm Wrack tilt and can still attack while Immobilized<br /> <br /> Apply it to the direct damage spells, boom! done.<br /> (Note, first Creative Thaumaturgying)</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that for some spells, eg Forces, holding the actual force instead of the charged spell, even momentarily, explicitly can hurt you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T02:18:04-08:00","id":1010984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1010983#post1010983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that for some spells, eg Forces, holding the actual force instead of the charged spell, even momentarily, explicitly can hurt you.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">+1 Reach: Create a 'physical' manifestation of the spell that attacks using Desterity+Weaponry/Brawl-Defense, extra successes does not add to the damage dealt. Split Potency between damage and uses, uses are drained when succesfully attacks and then decides to do damage, simply touching it does nothing. Using it in sensory range allows you to attack from range but still requires an attack roll but do not apply penalties to it from the Arm Wrack tilt and can still attack while Immobilized</span></i></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:19:36-08:00","id":1010989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>backtoback</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1010984#post1010984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">+1 Reach: Create a 'physical' manifestation of the spell that attacks using Desterity+Weaponry/Brawl-Defense, extra successes does not add to the damage dealt. Split Potency between damage and uses, uses are drained when succesfully attacks and then decides to do damage, simply touching it does nothing. Using it in sensory range allows you to attack from range but still requires an attack roll but do not apply penalties to it from the Arm Wrack tilt and can still attack while Immobilized</span></i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to allow a single reach effect to completely bypass one of the primary reasons for the Forces 4 attainment, and ignore the fact that every single published Forces spell is missing any kind of Reach effect saying that 'simply holding the energy doesn't hurt you', then yeah, that's a valid solution to do so. IMO, the existence of the attainment, clarification that Forces can still explicitly hurt you without it, and complete and total lack of any similar Reach effect in published Forces spells, presents a pretty strong argument to not do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:26:34-08:00","id":1010992,"title":"","content":"I would create a new spell for the &quot;Weaponized Thing&quot; thing. Mostly because each spell should be a very specific thing, and this is conceptually different enough to vary a new spell. And you don't need all that extra text you wrote; spell could be pretty much simplified to &quot;Create a PotencyRating Melee/Thrown Weapon that lasts [X] uses. This weapon deals Bashing damage.&quot; This should be pretty much universal for all Arcanas, and you can slap in arcana-specific options as Reach, usually in a form of tilt. The trade off between this and simply using a normal fraying spell would be efficiency (you spell cast once, and get multiple instances of the effect out of it), ability to convert to-hit into damage, and possibly ability to use it with Fighting Styles. instead of creating multiple exceptions to already exception-bloating system, you can just smoothly move to standard weapon rules (and yes, that would mean Strength to attack unless Finesse). <br /> <br /> If you want to be a Lightning-Slinger before Forces 4, just keep a Shielding spell on yourself beforehand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:37:42-08:00","id":1010994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906873#post906873\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906873#post906873\"> Creative Thaumaturgy: Fallen World Edition - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906873#post906873\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906873#post906873 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> With the advent of Awakening's Second Edition. I want to once again create a new thread in which to create, discuss, and critique new spells. Let this be that </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There was a discussion about weaponizing forces. On the same page you can find a few other itterations of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:57:10-08:00","id":1011207,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the idea of allowing 1 reach to add successes from the aiming roll to damage. Too broken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11839-cofdave","name":"CofDave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:43:59-08:00","id":1011254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofDave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1011207#post1011207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of like the idea of allowing 1 reach to add successes from the aiming roll to damage. Too broken?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is too broken, personally, but I can see how you could make an argument for it. Maybe for two reach? <br /> <br /> I have yet to play 2E mage but I like the aimed spell mechanic. Maybe houserule it so that wands add +1 to the roll to hit an aimed spell (which is presumably why mages use wands!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T18:30:29-08:00","id":1011295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1011254#post1011254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is too broken, personally, but I can see how you could make an argument for it. Maybe for two reach? <br /> <br /> I have yet to play 2E mage but I like the aimed spell mechanic. Maybe houserule it so that wands add +1 to the roll to hit an aimed spell (which is presumably why mages use wands!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wands (and other tools) generally add dice to casting rolls, though I can kind of see adding to aiming rolls if you want","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11839-cofdave","name":"CofDave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T18:42:38-08:00","id":1011299,"title":"","content":"Yeah, basically I would propose that wands are a special kind of tool that give a bonus to aiming spells. It seems kind of a natural extension of their function. An iron coin can be a great dedicated tool but is not necessarily going to help you land a spell, whereas an iron wand might.<br /> <br /> I would personally allow anything wandlike to fulfill this role, screwdrivers, pens, flashlights, rulers, etc, as long as it follows the existing rules for magical tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T19:49:50-08:00","id":1011318,"title":"","content":"From the Yantras section on page 121:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rods, wands, or staves are symbols of control \u2014 the ability to point and have a thing happen. Pointing a rod is a way of singling out a specific victim, while holding one is a symbol of rulership and command. It\u2019s also used as a symbol of male sexuality. </div> </div> </div>In short, what wands do is function as Tool Yantras for spells that target specific victims. Pretty much, any spell you would want to aim, a Wand can give a +1 on the spellcasting roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T20:18:27-08:00","id":1011327,"title":"","content":"I'm aware that wands can add to the spellcasting roll, I'm just suggesting they should also add to the spell aiming roll, which is a separate roll of gnosis + athletics/firearms - defense. Currently as written they don't provide that benefit, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T20:25:24-08:00","id":1011329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1011327#post1011327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware that wands can add to the spellcasting roll, I'm just suggesting they should also add to the spell aiming roll, which is a separate roll of gnosis + athletics/firearms - defense. Currently as written they don't provide that benefit, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see why they should. The symbolism of using a tool to indicate a target can help construct an imago, but pointing a stick at someone doesn't actually improve your aim any more than pointing your finger at them does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:17:16-08:00","id":1011421,"title":"","content":"I agree that magical tools shouldn't automatically grant an aiming benefit, but perhaps a spell could be cast on the tool (or even a wand that isn't used as a Yantra) to grant it an equipment bonus for aiming spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:21:30-08:00","id":1011422,"title":"","content":"To borrow a line from Charlaquin...<br /> &quot;Sounds like a good idea for a Merit&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though I totally can see a homerule where Wands have special affinity towards aimed spells if you want to specifically make Wand-using a Major Thing, like in Potterverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T05:03:50-08:00","id":1011456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010906-aimed-spells-and-successes?p=1011422#post1011422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To borrow a line from Charlaquin...<br /> &quot;Sounds like a good idea for a Merit&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though I totally can see a homerule where Wands have special affinity towards aimed spells if you want to specifically make Wand-using a Major Thing, like in Potterverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, something like this would make a good merit. Perhaps even a Style merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}